# Keep the build context small and keep local secrets out of the image.
#
# Note on patterns: a bare `.env` matches only the repository root. Every credential rule
# below is written `**/...` as well, because a key checked into a subdirectory is exactly
# the one nobody remembers is there.

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Virtual environments — the image builds its own at /app/.venv.
.venv
venv
env
**/.venv

__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
**/*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.coverage
htmlcov
build
dist

# --- never build a credential into an image -------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.key
**/*.key
*.p12
**/*.p12
*.pfx
**/*.pfx
*-key.json
**/*-key.json
service-account*.json
**/service-account*.json
application_default_credentials.json
**/application_default_credentials.json
.netrc
**/.netrc
.aws
.config
gha-creds-*.json

# --- not needed at runtime -------------------------------------------------------------
# The runtime image copies README.md (pyproject references it) and claude.md (the project
# constitution). `docs/` is *not* excluded, but only the test stage copies it: two tests
# assert that docs/A2A.md still says what the code does, and a test that cannot read the
# document it audits does not pass — it errors, which is a different and less useful thing.
# `*.md` matches root-level markdown only, so docs/*.md is unaffected by it.
DEMO.md
*.md
!README.md
!claude.md

Dockerfile
.dockerignore

captures
*.capture.json
runs
trace.json

.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
